# Operation Borderless walkthrough for the VS Code REST Client or the JetBrains HTTP client.
# Run the requests from top to bottom: later ones read ids from earlier responses.
# The same steps run unattended with `yarn demo`.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### 1a. Create wallet A
# @name createA
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/wallets
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ada@example.com" }

### 1b. Create wallet B
# @name createB
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/wallets
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "bayo@example.com" }

### 2. Deposit 1,000,000 cNGN into A (simulated)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/wallets/{{createA.response.body.id}}/deposits
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-deposit-1

{ "currency": "cNGN", "amount": "1000000" }

### 3. Swap 100,000 cNGN to USDx
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/wallets/{{createA.response.body.id}}/swaps
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-swap-1

{ "from_currency": "cNGN", "to_currency": "USDx", "amount": "100000" }

### 4. Cross-currency transfer: 50,000 cNGN from A to B, received as cGHS
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/wallets/{{createA.response.body.id}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-transfer-1

{
  "to_wallet_id": "{{createB.response.body.id}}",
  "source_currency": "cNGN",
  "destination_currency": "cGHS",
  "amount": "50000"
}

### 5. Replay step 4 with the same key: same body, Idempotent-Replayed: true
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/wallets/{{createA.response.body.id}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-transfer-1

{
  "to_wallet_id": "{{createB.response.body.id}}",
  "source_currency": "cNGN",
  "destination_currency": "cGHS",
  "amount": "50000"
}

### 6. Overdraft: 422 INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/wallets/{{createA.response.body.id}}/swaps
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-overdraft-1

{ "from_currency": "cNGN", "to_currency": "USDx", "amount": "10000000" }

### 7a. A's history, newest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/wallets/{{createA.response.body.id}}/transactions

### 7b. Current rates (simulated feed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/fx/rates

### 7c. Reconciliation (admin, unauthenticated)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/admin/reconciliation/run?mode=full

### Bonus: lock a rate for 30 seconds, then swap with it exactly once
# @name quote
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/fx/quotes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "wallet_id": "{{createA.response.body.id}}",
  "from_currency": "cNGN",
  "to_currency": "USDx",
  "amount": "1500"
}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/wallets/{{createA.response.body.id}}/swaps
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-quoted-swap-1

{
  "from_currency": "cNGN",
  "to_currency": "USDx",
  "amount": "1500",
  "quote_id": "{{quote.response.body.quote_id}}"
}
